ors  who've been infected have infected many  others within their healthcare community  and patients so this is a serious fear  issue in terms of even controlling  spread and preventing deaths we heard  from Michael Geary Valley on the program  who was talking about more protective  equipment being on its way clearly it's  a Herculean effort to get this amount of  protective equipment to the frontline as  the house secretary said but there have  also been stories or warnings if you  like that some hospitals and some areas  of the country could be running out  within days what is the reality we want  the government last weekend that there  were critically low shortages of full  sleeve gowns so they have notice of this  problem because as the BMA we have  reports from doctors across the UK but  what's really sort of frustrating and  remember our survey also showed that 51  percent of doctors don't feel looked  after by the government they don't feel  confident of being supported because at  the beginning of this pandemic we were  assured that the UK had sufficient  stockpiles you remember those  announcements being made and we believed  that we were well catered for we then  heard that the issues were not about the  stockpile but about operational  deliveries and we heard some apologies  that those deliveries had been the cause  of lack of supplies on the frontline now  we're being told we don't even have the  supplies so it's really difficult  because we're not being given clear  information doctors are going in to work  every day just not knowing whether they  will have the equipment to protect them  and remember this is you know we are  talking about particular equipment that  is life-saving for for doctors and for  the patient's they care after we've been  talking a lot in the program about  whether the UK responds to coronavirus  has been slow you on the show a month  ago when you said that we don't have the  luxury of time to prepare for this  crisis anymore do 